From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:29:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: nt37280-lh568wf3: take over the bootloader's panel
 without a reset

The probe held the panel in reset and prepare pulsed it again. With
ABL's splash now scanning out until msm's first frame (dispcc keeps the
MDP clock), that reset is what would blank the screen at the panel's
probe instead. When the bootloader left the panel out of reset, keep it
as is the first time; it goes on showing the splash until msm's first
frame.

Not the colour-block frame at boot, though it was written for it: that
was dispcc parking the MDP clock under the scanout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../panel/panel-lg-nt37280-lh568wf3-ed01.c    | 20 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-nt37280-lh568wf3-ed01.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-nt37280-lh568wf3-ed01.c
index 3041b89701ff..d5a124a8b92e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-nt37280-lh568wf3-ed01.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-nt37280-lh568wf3-ed01.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ struct nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01 {
 	struct drm_dsc_config dsc;
 	struct regulator_bulk_data *supplies;
 	struct gpio_desc *reset_gpio;
+	bool handover;
 };
 
 static const struct regulator_bulk_data nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_supplies[] = {
@@ -144,7 +145,14 @@ static int nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_reset(ctx);
+	/*
+	 * A reset blanks the panel's frame memory, and display on would
+	 * show that until the first frame comes. Keep the bootloader's
+	 * panel, still showing its splash, the first time.
+	 */
+	if (!ctx->handover)
+		nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_reset(ctx);
+	ctx->handover = false;
 
 	ret = nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_on(ctx);
 	if (ret < 0) {
@@ -286,11 +294,19 @@ static int nt37280_lh568wf3_ed01_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	ctx->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	ctx->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "reset", GPIOD_ASIS);
 	if (IS_ERR(ctx->reset_gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(ctx->reset_gpio),
 				     "Failed to get reset-gpios\n");
 
+	/* Out of reset: the bootloader left the panel on */
+	ctx->handover = !gpiod_get_value_cansleep(ctx->reset_gpio);
+	ret = gpiod_direction_output(ctx->reset_gpio, !ctx->handover);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	if (ctx->handover)
+		dev_info(dev, "taking over the bootloader's panel\n");
+
 	ctx->dsi = dsi;
 	mipi_dsi_set_drvdata(dsi, ctx);
 
